  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MainMenuData
  gameTitle: CHATURANGA
  startRunLabel: Start Run
  infoLabel: Info
  optionsLabel: Options
  exitLabel: Exit
  infoTitle: How to Play
  pieceSheet:
  - {fileID: -5619150752979459227, guid: 6603f81f61c69b547b2a0b5cde0d8619, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -5619150752979459227, guid: 6603f81f61c69b547b2a0b5cde0d8619, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -5619150752979459227, guid: 6603f81f61c69b547b2a0b5cde0d8619, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -5619150752979459227, guid: 6603f81f61c69b547b2a0b5cde0d8619, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -5619150752979459227, guid: 6603f81f61c69b547b2a0b5cde0d8619, type: 3}
  - {fileID: -5619150752979459227, guid: 6603f81f61c69b547b2a0b5cde0d8619, type: 3}
  overviewText: Chaturanga is a roguelike tactical chess game. Each run you select
    and command a squad of chess pieces through escalating fights. After three fights
    you can enter the MainFrame code and buy pieces, relics and floppies; you can
    also upgrade your existing pieces. Defeat the enemy squad to win a fight.
  runStructureText: "A run follows a repeating cycle:\n\nFIGHT \u2014 Face an enemy
    squad on a chess board. You and the AI alternate turns. Eliminate all enemy pieces
    to win. Your pieces carry over to the next fight.\n\nVICTORY REWARD \u2014 You
    get Bits for winning, bits for time not spent and bits for alive pieces.\n\nMAINFRAME
    MARKET \u2014 Spend Bits to buy stuff. The market re-rolls its selection every
    time you visit.\n\nYou may upgrade as many types as you can afford before entering
    the next fight.\n\nManaging your Bits wisely is the key to surviving deeper into
    a run."
  pieces:
  - pieceName: Pawn
    sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 13917c55ada907d44b4c4a8dda213674, type: 3}
    accentColor: {r: 0.4, g: 0.8, b: 0.55, a: 1}
    moveText: Moves forward one square. Captures diagonally forward.
    upgradeText: "Double Step \u2014 can advance two squares from any rank as long
      as both squares ahead are empty."
  - pieceName: Rook
    sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 982b3665c89c50a4d9d1f71eb37731da, type: 3}
    accentColor: {r: 0.35, g: 0.65, b: 0.95, a: 1}
    moveText: Slides any number of squares along ranks or files (horizontal or vertical).
    upgradeText: "Phase Charge \u2014 phases straight through enemy Pawns without
      capturing them, continuing its slide."
  - pieceName: Knight
    sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0e8adb60126a21b48b0d3f05ec315ff6, type: 3}
    accentColor: {r: 0.75, g: 0.5, b: 0.95, a: 1}
    moveText: 'Leaps in an L-shape (2 squares + 1 to the side). Jumps over all other
      pieces. '
    upgradeText: "Extended Leap \u2014 gains an additional (3+1) leap range on top
      of its normal moves."
  - pieceName: Bishop
    sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: db977a39575d41944b1a4a4a8fb27454, type: 3}
    accentColor: {r: 0.95, g: 0.8, b: 0.3, a: 1}
    moveText: Slides diagonally any number of squares. Stays on its starting color.
    upgradeText: "Cross-step \u2014 after completing a diagonal slide it may take
      one additional step in a cardinal direction."
  - pieceName: Queen
    sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a4c98690244894c47b237081190b1824, type: 3}
    accentColor: {r: 0.95, g: 0.45, b: 0.7, a: 1}
    moveText: Slides any number of squares in all 8 directions. The most powerful
      piece on the board.
    upgradeText: "Compound Strike \u2014 after capturing an enemy piece the Queen
      retreats one step back along the same attack ray."
  - pieceName: King
    sprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5b569ebf269b79b40b5a8aca9fd9ced5, type: 3}
    accentColor: {r: 0.95, g: 0.6, b: 0.25, a: 1}
    moveText: Moves one square in any direction. If your King is captured, the run
      ends immediately.
    upgradeText: "Armor Guard \u2014 at the start of each player turn the King grants
      1 Armor to the three pieces directly in front of it."
  armorText: "A piece with Armor absorbs one fatal hit instead of dying.\nWhen the
    Armor is lost the piece survives but is Stunned \u2014 you cant move it next
    turn.\nKnights always pierce Armor and deal damage directly to the piece beneath.\nArmor
    is shown by a shield icon above the pieces."
  suddenDeathText: "Triggers when neither side can make progress \u2014 either a
    1v1 stand-off or too many consecutive rounds with no capture.\n\nEach Sudden
    Death round, one edge strip of tiles is highlighted red. After the AI completes
    its turn, that strip collapses: every piece on it is destroyed and those tiles
    are permanently removed from play.\n\nCollapse order: left column \u2192 bottom
    row \u2192 right column \u2192 top row \u2192 repeat inward.\n\nSudden Death
    forces a decisive result \u2014 there are no draws in Chaturanga."
  floppyIntroText: "Floppies are single-use abilities you activate during a fight.
    Each one has an immediate effect \u2014 stun an enemy, armor a piece, move again
    \u2014 and is consumed once used.\n\nYou collect floppies in two ways: Random
    free reward after each victory, or buying them from the Mainframe Market between
    fights."
  floppies:
  - floppyName: Armor
    cost: 3
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: Apply 1 Armor stack to a friendly piece. That piece will survive
      its next lethal hit and be Stunned instead of dying. Has no effect if the piece
      already has Armor.
  - floppyName: Retreat
    cost: 2
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: Move a friendly piece one square toward your back rank (downward).
      Useful to pull a threatened piece out of danger. Does nothing if the square
      behind is occupied or out of bounds.
  - floppyName: Stun
    cost: 3
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: Stun an enemy piece for one turn. It will skip its move entirely
      during the next AI turn. Combine with Hack for a guaranteed lost turn.
  - floppyName: Upgrade
    cost: 4
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: Temporarily upgrade a friendly piece for the duration of this fight
      only. The upgrade is lost when the fight ends. Cannot be used on a piece that
      is already upgraded.
  - floppyName: Hack
    cost: 4
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: "Hack an enemy piece. On the next AI turn that piece is the only
      one that can move \u2014 the rest of the enemy squad is locked. If the hacked
      piece is also stunned the AI loses its turn entirely."
  - floppyName: Ethereal
    cost: 3
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: Make a friendly piece ethereal for one turn. It can move through
      friendly pieces as if they were not there, opening otherwise blocked paths.
      The effect expires at the end of the turn.
  - floppyName: Morph
    cost: 5
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: Temporarily transform a friendly piece into a Queen for one full
      turn. The original piece is hidden and restored at the start of the next player
      turn. The queen inherits the piece's Armor and upgrade state.
  - floppyName: Dismantle
    cost: 0
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: Sacrifice a friendly piece to earn 10 Bits immediately. The piece
      is removed from the board permanently. Useful for converting a weak or stranded
      piece into economy.
  - floppyName: Ctrl+Z
    cost: 3
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: "Revert the board to the state from two half-turns ago \u2014 undoing
      both the AI's last move and your own previous turn. A confirm dialog appears
      before the revert executes. Cannot be used if there is no history to revert
      to."
  - floppyName: Wall
    cost: 3
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d81924d4fe26fd74f97044a7be54a4be, type: 3}
    description: "Select up to 3 connected empty tiles to wall off. During the next
      AI turn those tiles are blocked \u2014 enemy pieces cannot move onto or through
      them. The wall is shown as a red danger highlight and is removed after the
      AI moves."
  discIntroText: "Discs are permanent items you carry for the entire run. Unlike
    floppies they are never consumed \u2014 once you have a disc its effect is always
    active. Discs are found in the Mainframe Market and earned in random events ir
    killing Chess Masters."
  discs: []
  infoBackLabel: Back
  optionsBackLabel: Back
